<div id='content'>
<h1>positron</h1>

<p>
This is the home of positron, the synchronization manager for the Neuros Audio Computer.  This software is primarily intended to support Linux, but will probably be portable to other POSIX systems such as OS X and the BSDs. Currently there are USB protocol issues with OS X, so please don’t try it there yet.
</p>

<h2 id="vorbis">Vorbis support</h2>
<p>Vorbis support is now standard on current Neuros firmwares, so positron
will default to enabling Vorbis support.  You will still need to do the 
following:</p>
<ul>

	<li>Install pyogg and pyvorbis.  These can be found on the <a
	href="http://www.andrewchatham.com/pyogg/">pyogg site</a>, or they
	might already be packaged by your distribution.</li>
	<li>If you already used the positron 1.0 release, you may need to
	edit <code>~/.positron/config</code> and remove the option 
	<code>oggvorbis_support=false</code>.</li>
</ul>


<h2>Latest Release: 1.1</h2>

<p>
This release includes proper track sorting for albums and much improved
MP3 detection.  We recommend you
run <code>positron rebuild</code> to fix the sorting.  Check out the
<a href="files/ChangeLog">ChangeLog</a> for a complete list of updates.
</p>

<h3>Source Downloads</h3>
<p><a href="files/source/positron-1.1.tar.gz">positron-1.1.tar.gz</a> - Source Tarball</p>

<h3>Binary Downloads</h3>

<p>None yet!  Feel free to contribute some!</p>

